# localclaw - secret injection map (SAMPLE, non-secret).
#
# This file maps environment variables that the foreground OpenClaw gateway
# needs to secret references. It contains ONLY names and references -- never
# the secret values themselves.
#
# scripts/bootstrap copies this to:
#   ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/localclaw/secrets.map
#
# In SECRET_BACKEND=vault mode, use (whitespace separated):
#   ENV_VAR_NAME   <kv-path-under-mount>   <field>
#
# The KV path is relative to your KV v2 mount (VAULT_KV_MOUNT, default
# "local"). For example the line below reads the "api_key" field from
# "local/ai/anthropic" and exports it as ANTHROPIC_API_KEY into the
# foreground gateway only. work-session never writes these values to disk,
# logs, or command-line arguments.
#
# In SECRET_BACKEND=password-manager mode, the second column is a provider
# reference and the third column is password or notes. Store the corresponding
# values in the configured provider. Provider references must not contain
# whitespace. Example:
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY   LocalClaw Anthropic API   password
#   OPENAI_API_KEY      LocalClaw OpenAI API      notes
#
# Store Vault secrets during a work session, e.g.:
#   LOCAL_VAULT_TOKEN=... vault kv put local/ai/anthropic api_key=-   # prompts
#
# Remove or add lines to match the providers you actually use. If your
# OpenClaw build reads its API keys from its own config instead of the
# environment, you may leave this file empty.

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY   ai/anthropic   api_key
OPENAI_API_KEY      ai/openai      api_key
